B = [
('Fisher-Price','North America','1950s-present','toys','In the style of Fisher-Price, chunky rounded forms with thick softened corners and no sharp edges anywhere. Materials are glossy moulded plastic and warm lacquered wood with slightly worn paint. Palette is primary red, sunny yellow, cobalt blue and grass green against clean white and natural pale timber. Flat lithographed decoration shows simple smiling faces made from two dots and a curve, little cartoon animals and dotted rim details in a naive hand-drawn manner. Round peg-like silhouettes, oval badges and big circles repeat as a motif. Lettering is rounded, friendly and lowercase-leaning, set in white on a bold red band or oval emblem. Everything feels sturdy, cheerful, safe and handmade-simple.'),
('Sanrio','East Asia','1970s-present','design language','In the style of Sanrio, kawaii softness built from round, plump, pillow-like shapes with tiny black dot eyes set wide apart and almost no features. Outlines are thin, even and gentle with flat fills. Palette is pastel pink, baby blue, lavender, mint, butter yellow and clean white, with a single red or hot pink bow-like accent. Surfaces are glossy, satin or glittery with a candy-sweet sheen, in translucent plastic, plush fleece and shiny paper. Scattered hearts, stars, tiny fruit and flowers form repeating confetti patterns on pale grounds. Lettering is bubbly, rounded and childlike, often with a small heart or star dotting the letters. Generous empty space keeps every layout light, sweet and tidy.'),
('Aardman','Europe','1980s-present','design language','In the style of Aardman, hand-sculpted modelling clay forms with soft lumpy volumes, visible thumbprints and tool marks, and a slightly matte waxy skin. Shapes are squat, rounded and exaggerated, with big expressive eyes, wide toothy grins and chunky limbs, all deliberately a little wonky. Palette is warm and earthy with oatmeal beige, terracotta orange, mustard, moss green, dusty blue and off-white, plus the occasional vivid candy colour. Surfaces carry gentle crumpled seams and joins that celebrate handmade imperfection. Patterns lean on homely checks, florals and stripes in muted tones. Lettering is wobbly, rounded and hand-cut. Overall a cosy, witty, tactile and charmingly dishevelled craft character.'),
('Hanna-Barbera','North America','1950s-70s','design language','In the style of Hanna-Barbera, flat limited-colour cartoon design with confident thick dark outlines and solid fills with almost no shading. Shapes are simple, blocky and rounded, with big ovals, wide stylised noses and bold geometric simplification of anything natural. Palette is mid-century saturated orange, turquoise, mustard, brick red, avocado green, sky blue and brown, often as loose painted blobs and speckled textures with a slightly gaudy retro charm. Repeating motifs include stylised rocks, leaves and zigzag stone patterns. Lettering is chunky, hand-drawn, slightly uneven and outlined, often arched or stacked inside a bright emblem with a rainbow swirl ring or star. The look is breezy, cheeky and cheerfully retro.'),
('Taschen','Europe','1980s-present','design language','In the style of Taschen, bold, oversized and confidently sensual graphic design with a gallery-grade polish. Forms are large clean rectangles with crisp square edges and generous margins. Surfaces are thick matte or satin boards, linen, leatherette and glossy printed art, with foil stamping and embossing used sparingly. Palette is rich saturated colour, a single flat field of deep red, jet black, cream or electric yellow, set beside vivid full-bleed imagery of strong contrast. Lettering is tidy, modern sans-serif, small and spaced, in white or black, with a tiny wordmark in a corner. Layout is minimal, grid-based and tightly aligned, suggesting luxury, cult curiosity and pop-culture connoisseurship.'),
('Blue Note Records','North America','1950s-60s','design language','In the style of Blue Note Records, modernist mid-century graphic design with a cool, smoky, rhythmic feel. Compositions are asymmetrical and built on strict grids, with tightly cropped duotone imagery in deep blue, black and white, interrupted by flat blocks of orange, red, yellow, cyan or green. Lettering is bold, condensed or heavy sans-serif, set large, tilted, stacked and sometimes overlapping, with letters bleeding off an edge and lines of text rotated ninety degrees. Thin rules, circles, dots and angular bars add rhythm. Surfaces are matte ink on slightly textured paper with grainy halftone texture and visible overprint. The emblem is a small blue circle with a rounded lowercase wordmark.'),
('Heineken','Europe','1960s-present','design language','In the style of Heineken, crisp, confident, premium European branding in deep emerald green with bright signal red and white. A bold red five-pointed star is the central repeatable emblem, set inside a round or oval seal edged with fine white and silver outlines, with a small crest-like ring of tiny text. Lettering is lowercase, rounded sans-serif in white with a gently tilted letter e, also seen in solid green on white. Finishes are glossy lacquer, brushed silver foil and embossed metallic details with a lustrous sheen. Layouts are clean and uncluttered, with large flat green fields, thin red accents and oversized cropped lettering used as pattern. The mood is fresh, polished and international.'),
('Cadbury','Europe','1900s-present','design language','In the style of Cadbury, a rich deep royal purple dominates every surface in a glossy, silky, velvety finish. The signature mark is a flowing hand-written gold script in thick looping letters, set inside a soft rounded oval or swooping ribbon swirl. Cream, white and warm gold act as accents, along with thin gold borders, curved swoosh lines and ribbon-like flowing shapes. Surfaces include metallic gold foil, satin paper and smooth lacquer with a soft highlight. Shapes are rounded, plump and generous, with gently curved corners and sweeping curves rather than angles. Decorative flourishes, swirls and subtle shimmer add a sense of treat and indulgence. The mood is warm, traditional, comforting and generous.'),
('Toblerone','Europe','1900s-present','design language','In the style of Toblerone, forms built from repeating triangular peaks, like a row of snowy mountains, with sawtooth silhouettes, sloping sides and crisp faceted geometry. Palette is warm honey gold, cream yellow and sunlit tan, with deep red, dark brown and navy accents on white. Surfaces are matte card, satin foil and light embossing with a clean tactile finish. Lettering is tall, sturdy, outlined serif capitals with subtle shadow, often sitting in a long horizontal band. The emblem is a mountain silhouette in solid gold or yellow, with a hidden bear shape tucked into its negative space. Triangular tessellations, stepped zigzag borders and tidy geometric rhythm create an Alpine, wholesome and cleverly witty personality.'),
('Haribo','Europe','1920s-present','design language','In the style of Haribo, bright, cheerful, playful German retro fun. Palette is glossy primary red, sunshine yellow, orange, lime green and clear sky blue, with metallic gold foil and deep black outlines for contrast. Materials are translucent jelly-like gloss, crinkly shiny metallic film and clear windows showing a jumble of small chunky shapes, soft, smooth and slightly sugar-dusted. Lettering is bold, rounded, capitalised and set in red with a heavy black outline and white edge, often arched over a golden mascot-like cartoon figure with a friendly smile and a red neck bow. Forms are small, plump, rounded and simple. Colour does the shouting, and the whole language feels sunny, sweet, nostalgic and instantly readable.'),
]
